#backblast #f3_strongest_pax #IBsWereCrushed #Ellory_is_our_heart_Warrior!

June, 20th 2026

Once again, we did the thing. We gathered together as an F3 community of guys that love to compete and LIFT HEAVY STUFF!  On top of that, we were able to benefit children born with Congenital Heart Defects, and their families. I cannot thank the guys that helped put this together enough, because without you, this never happens. F3 truly is an amalgam of men that pour into each other and their communities. We are blessed.

HUGE thank you to Stephanie and Robby McDaniel. They turned the tragic loss of their baby boy into a movement to try and ensure that other families do not have to endure the pain that they did, and frankly still do. It is because of them that we have the ability to assist in such a glorious mission. We will keep the donation pathways open until it gets closer to the time to buy a sponsorship, but we should end up right around $5500 in total donations (about $2000 more than last year)!!!!

The icing on the cake is that a lot of men got to push themselves past their own perceived limits. There wasn't a single one of us that wasn't nervous about this competition. It didn't matter if you thought you could win, or if you were just hoping to survive, these events change you. That is part of what F3 is all about. We are a community of men, doing what we can to show each other, and ourselves, that we can be fitter, faster, stronger, and more importantly better leaders within our communities. I personally hope that everyone, that competed in this event, carries a sense of pride for putting themselves into an uncomfortable position and coming out on the other side.

There were also some surprise heroes. Huge thank you to my M (Allison), my 2.0 @Near Fall, my 2.1 @powder burn (He flaked out half way because we are boring), @Captain America, and @Bobwire (MKT). The gave a lot of their time and even sacrificed a tractor tire. It was hot, and miserable for the competitors, but our volunteers and families had to deal with it all too. Without all of their support, we don't get to be who were are. My M puts up with a lot of my shenanigans, and this event is certainly one of them. However, she always jumps to help and never forgets to give me a hard time about it.  (Please reference the picture of her hat. LOL)

